<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siemowit IV of Masovia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1352–1426</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siemowit IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> was a Piast duke of Masovia and a candidate for the Polish throne in 1382. He married Alexandra, sister of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a>, and in 1388 received the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belz">Belz</a> as a fief, beginning the Masovian line that held it until 1462.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siemowit-iv-of-masovia.jpg" alt="Siemowit IV of Masovia" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franciszek Piekosiński · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siemowit_IV,_Duke_of_Masovia_seal_(16841461).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
